Trails:
Trails within this Wild Area are some of the steepest and most rugged found in the Elk State Forest and northcentral Pennsylvania. Hikers are reminded to know their limitations!

Square Timber Trail…7.4 miles… approximately 1,200’ of elevation change;

Big Run Trail (section)…1.7 miles…approximately 100’ of elevation;

Big Run Right Fork Trail (section)…1.6 miles… approximately 900’ of elevation;

Big Run Left Fork Trail (section)…2 miles… approximately 1,000’ of elevation;

Bucktail Path…2.2 miles… approximately 300’ of elevation change

Each trailhead can accommodate 2 to 3 vehicles.
